# {{.project_name}}

Fullstack workspace generated by smokeforge.

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `apps/api` | Go or Rust API; owns persistence, auth, and business rules |
| `apps/web` | Next.js frontend; owns UI and the `/api/auth/*` BFF |
| `deploy/` | Reserved for deployment assets |
| `CONTEXT-MAP.md` | Where to find project context and boundaries |

## First run

```bash
make install
make api-dev   # API on http://localhost:8080
make web-dev   # web on http://localhost:3000
```

Docker:

```bash
make docker-up
```

The web app talks to the API through its same-origin BFF. Browser code never
receives the API access or refresh token. Set `API_URL` for the Next.js server
and `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` for the browser origin. See
[CONTEXT-MAP.md](CONTEXT-MAP.md) before changing authentication or data flow.
